# The vendored axe build is checked byte-for-byte against a hash recorded in
# clauditseo/vendor/README.md. Line-ending normalisation would rewrite it on
# checkout and fail that check on a fresh clone — on Windows especially,
# which is where most of this is run.
#
# These paths said `auditdeck/` for ten audit rounds after the rename, so the
# rule parsed, matched nothing and protected nothing. `git check-attr` is the
# only thing that can tell the difference, which is what the test asserts.
clauditseo/vendor/axe.min.js -text
clauditseo/vendor/axe-core-LICENSE.txt -text

# The prompts are installed verbatim from the operator's relay attachments, and
# at least one is held to that byte for byte
# (`tests/test_the_links_brief.py::test_the_prompt_is_the_one_the_operator_supplied`).
# The reason differs from the vendored blob above: not a recorded hash, but an
# attachment the operator asked to be installed unchanged. Normalisation rewrote
# them to CRLF on checkout while the attachments hold LF, so the comparison
# failed on the first newline in every fresh clone and every new worktree, and
# passed for whoever still had the old file on disk (item 170).
#
# All of them, not only the compared one: the broad rule is simpler and leaves
# no trap for the next prompt held to its attachment.
clauditseo/prompts/*.md -text

# --- what a public export leaves behind (item 187) -------------------------
#
# `PUBLIC_EXCLUDE.txt` is the manifest, with a reason beside every line. These
# are the same paths expressed the way `git archive` understands, so the
# packaging script - which builds from `git archive HEAD` precisely so that
# git, not a glob in a shell script, decides what ships - leaves them out
# without being told twice.
#
# `tests/test_no_client_data_ships.py` holds these two lists to each other, so
# a path added to one and forgotten in the other fails rather than leaks.
audits/ export-ignore
OPERATOR_ACTIONS.md export-ignore
QUESTIONS.md export-ignore
NEXT_UP.md export-ignore
BACKLOG.md export-ignore
TIMINGS.md export-ignore
benchmarks/reports/ export-ignore
benchmarks/results.jsonl export-ignore
.client-tokens export-ignore
